      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "EXPERIMENTAL TOOLS\n\nUpload an original clip and matching full-scene inverse depth. Set the point and reference frame before running. Chain more EF Mask Point nodes to include/exclude objects, or disconnect positive points to use include words. Red = excluded, green = emission source. Nothing downloads automatically."
      ],
      "color": "#454024",
      "bgcolor": "#292719"
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1130,
        20
      ],
      "size": [
        1360,
        170
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 16,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "EMISSION IS NOT SCENE VISIBILITY\n\nThe selection mask limits particle births. Keep the full depth map connected for scene interaction. guide_content only changes what LTX sees. To use full scene, choose full object instead of inner edge. Inspect word exclusions: SAM may select an unintended object. See docs/particle-depth.md."
      ],
      "color": "#454024",
      "bgcolor": "#292719"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        30,
        1260
      ],
      "size": [
        1000,
        230
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 17,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "CONNECT TO YOUR LTX / COMPOSITING WORKFLOW\n\nMerged guide goes to one IC-LoRA reference. Object and particle outputs can feed two references. This example does not generate video. Optional effect_visibility goes to EF Place Layer holdout; protected goes to EF Restore Protected Object after glow when exact original pixels are required. Protect a broader object than the emission source if needed."
      ],
      "color": "#454024",
      "bgcolor": "#292719"
    }
